# Git

- The repository root is the workspace root `Firebird-test/`, with no nested project folder. The task PDF in the root is not committed (`*.pdf` in `.gitignore`).
- History is linear on `main`; optional short branches `stage-<n>-<topic>` are merged by fast-forward.
- Conventional Commits in English: `type(scope): summary`.
  - Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `perf`, `build`, `chore`, `docs`.
  - Scope: an FSD slice or area.
  - Imperative summary, at most 72 characters; the body cites requirement IDs and the stage.
- One logical change per commit, together with its docs and prompt-log entry.
- Hooks: `pre-commit` runs lint-staged (ESLint on staged files) and `npm run typecheck`, `pre-push` runs `npm run verify`. Never `--no-verify` or `HUSKY=0`.
- Commit `package-lock.json`, `Gemfile.lock`, `ios/Podfile.lock`. Ignore `node_modules`, `ios/Pods`, build outputs, `.env*`, logs, `*.pdf`.
- Commit AI artifacts: `docs/ai/prompts.md` entries and exports in `docs/ai/chats/`.
- Commit and push only when the user asks. No force-push to `main`, no rewriting pushed history, no secrets.

Checks:
- husky `pre-commit` and `pre-push` (installed in stage 2).
- Commit messages by review.

Full guide: @docs/ai/guidelines/git.md
